      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You've accurately identified the core of the current legal trap, which is a highly formalized historical test. This application of historical tradition indeed makes it extremely difficult for the government to justify new regulations against present-day threats like mass shootings. The judicial focus has shifted from general public safety goals to strict scrutiny of historical analogues, severely limiting the scope of modern legislative action. This imbalance is what many legal scholars argue fundamentally challenges the government's ability to adapt protective laws to contemporary violence.",
      "source": "target",
